   "id": 614219,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "An electric current through hydrogen gas produces several distinct wavelengths of visible light. The light is projected onto a diffraction grating having <span data-math=\"10\\text{,}000\"></span> lines per centimeter. What are the wavelengths of the hydrogen spectrum if the light forms first-order maxima at angles of <span data-math=\"24.2^{\\circ}\">24.2^{\\circ}</span>, <span data-math=\"25.7^{\\circ}\">25.7^{\\circ}</span>, <span data-math=\"29.1^{\\circ}\">29.1^{\\circ}</span>, and <span data-math=\"41.0^{\\circ}\">41.0^{\\circ}</span>?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1164861,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\lambda_1=\\left(10^3\\,\\text{nm}\\right)\\sin 24.2^{\\circ}=410\\,\\text{nm}\">\\lambda_1=\\left(10^3\\,\\text{nm}\\right)\\sin 24.2^{\\circ}=410\\,\\text{nm}</span>\n <span data-math=\"\\lambda_2=\\left(10^3\\,\\text{nm}\\right)\\sin 25.7^{\\circ}=434\\,\\text{nm}\">\\lambda_2=\\left(10^3\\,\\text{nm}\\right)\\sin 25.7^{\\circ}=434\\,\\text{nm}</span>\n <span data-math=\"\\lambda_3=\\left(10^3\\,\\text{nm}\\right)\\sin 29.1^{\\circ}=486\\,\\text{nm}\">\\lambda_3=\\left(10^3\\,\\text{nm}\\right)\\sin 29.1^{\\circ}=486\\,\\text{nm}</span>\n <span data-math=\"\\lambda_4=\\left(10^3\\,\\text{nm}\\right)\\sin\n 41.0^{\\circ}=656\\,\\text{nm}\">\\lambda_4=\\left(10^3\\,\\text{nm}\\right)\\sin\n 41.0^{\\circ}=656\\,\\text{nm}</span>"
    },
